# Measuring harnesses. app/public/ is served by the dev server and ships
# with the build, which makes it the only convenient place to put a page
# that renders real components against the real stylesheet so their
# geometry can be read with getBoundingClientRect instead of guessed at
# from a screenshot. The zz- prefix marks those as scratch: they are how
# a number gets checked, not part of the app. Named rather than
# gitignoring the whole directory, which holds the icons and the
# manifest.
#
# This line only keeps them out of git. That is enough for Vercel, which
# builds from git, and it is not enough for the phone: a local
# `npm run build` copies public/ wholesale and `npx cap sync` carries the
# result into the iOS bundle, so the harnesses shipped in the only build
# a producer ever installs. Keeping them out of a build is a build's job,
# and app/vite.config.ts does it.
app/public/zz-*

# Screen recordings and screenshots dropped in for reference. They are
# how a design gets described; they are not source, and they are large.
*.MP4
*.mp4
*.mov
